{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>A little sleep</b> — in the language of the Rabbis. The meaning: you will sleep time after time; you will sleep a little and slumber a little and fold your hands so that you do not toil."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:09.890918505Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}